# Phase 4: the VMM hardens the kernel mappings at boot and passes its
# self-test (twice, to show nothing leaks between runs).
vmm: kernel space adopted; NX and WP on
vmm: image
cerberus kernel shell
!send test vmm
!wait 4
map/write/read/unmap: access after unmap faulted at 0x40000000 (not-present)
W+X requests rejected
kernel image: writes to .rodata and .text fault; a jump into .data faults
demand paging: 64 pages reserved, 4 touched, 4 frames allocated
zeroing: frame
came back all zero
mprotect: read-only pages refuse writes
munmap: hole punched
guard page: the page below the mapping is reserved and faults
copy-on-write: parent and child each see only their own write
2 MiB page: one huge leaf
teardown: all user frames freed
test vmm: PASS
!send test vmm
!wait 4
teardown: all user frames freed; 0 frame(s) kept
test vmm: PASS
